        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Become immersed in Cambodian culture and discover the history of Cambodia through painting, literary, and photo exhibitions, traditional dance and music performances, talks, as well as tastings of Cambodian dishes. Activities inspired by Asian traditions will also be offered, such as massage therapy, tattoos, and more.  Saturday, May 24  10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m.: Talk 1975, l’année des chutes, une perspective historique (1975, the Year of the Fall: A Historical Perspective)  11:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.: Roundtable 50 ans après : où en est la communauté du Sud-Est asiatique? (50 Years Later: Where is the Southeast Asian Community Today?), with Tito Kang (F3CM) et Linda Saphan 2 p.m. to 3 p.m.: Roundtable with Bryan Beyung and MU 3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m.: Vernissage with graffiti artist FONKI and guests  Sunday, May 25  1:30 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.: Roundtable on the representation of Asians in arts, culture, and media 3:00 p.m. to 4 p.m.: Conversation with arts industry professionals with the Festival Accès Asie 4:30 p.m. to 5:30 p.m.: Youth roundtable with sexologist Kanica 6:00 p.m.: Closing ceremony 6:30 p.m. to 8:30 p.m.: Asian open mic, special edition for the 2025 Festival Champa 8:30 p.m.: Launch of DI Soria's new album  Snacks prepared by Asian moms, gourmet bites created by Chef Chanthy Yen, exclusive cocktails, and Asian beverages will also be available for purchase on-site throughout the two days."
      }
    ],
